{
  "dom_id": "step-q262883",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Use a calculator to evaluate ${log}_{8}⁡(19)$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n${log}_{8}⁡(19)≈$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let's calculate ${log}_{8}⁡(19)$ by changing the base $8$ to the common logarithm (base $10$).\n\nWe use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=8,$ $X=19,$ $b=10.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{8}⁡(19) & =\\frac{{log}_{10}⁡(19)}{{log}_{10}⁡(8)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(19)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(8)} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{1.278\\,754}{0.903\\,090} \\\\  & ≈1.416\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
